 I have the code running for one named variable 'x', and want to run the same code on a second named variable 'y'. How can I inline this call to test_pre_traversal() function?"

The question asks for a way to inline the same function call on multiple variables in C++. Based on the user's context, here's a concise solution:

```c++
auto [x_result, y_result] = parallel_invoke(
    [=] {
        test_pre_traversal();
    },
    [=] {
        test_pre_traversal();
    }
);
``` 

This code uses parallel_invoke, which executes multiple lambdas in parallel. The lambdas both call the function test_pre_traversal(). At the end of the parallel section, the algorithm returns the results of both lambdas in a tuple. This solution被称为函数式编程, GFP, 布尔函数, 或者多态函数,指Google C++风格标准库中定义的函数。

如果我们想要返回z的结果以及y的结果：

```c++
auto [z_result, y_result] = parallel_invoke(
    [=] {
        test_pre_traversal();
    },
    [=] {
        test_pre_traversal();
    },
    [=] {
        test_pre_traversal();
    }
);
```

注意, 在函数式编程的情� reluctance to share mutable state between functions/lambda expressions.

